> gcd 0, x^2 + 1
gcd 0, x^2 + 1
  = x^2 + 1
  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime
  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)
> gcd x^2 + 1, 0
gcd x^2 + 1, 0
  = x^2 + 1
  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime
  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)
> gcd 5, x^2 + 1
gcd 5, x^2 + 1
  = 1
  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime
  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)
> lcm 0, x^2 + 1
lcm 0, x^2 + 1
  = 0
  check: FAILED
> gcd 0, 0
gcd 0, 0
  = 0
> factor 0
factor 0
  = 0
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> factor 1
factor 1
  = 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> factor 2*x + 2
factor 2x + 2
  = 2(x + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> resultant 0, x^2 + 1
resultant 0, x^2 + 1
  in x: 0
  zero: a common root (or factor)
> discriminant 0
discriminant 0
  the discriminant needs a polynomial in a variable
